When migrating legacy `timetable` data into `semesters`, an empty timetable object `{ '월': [], '화': [], ... }` is truthy, causing it to unconditionally overwrite `DEFAULT_SEMESTERS['1-1']` with empty data — leaving only the 1-1 semester blank while 2-1 through 4-2 retain defaults.

## Change

**`modules/schedule.js` — migration guard**

Add a `hasClasses` check before overwriting `defaultSemesters['1-1']`, so the migration only applies when the old timetable contains actual entries:

```javascript
const hasClasses = Object.values(this.settings.schedule.timetable).some(
    dayClasses => Array.isArray(dayClasses) && dayClasses.length > 0
);
if (hasClasses) {
    defaultSemesters['1-1'] = this.settings.schedule.timetable;
}
```

- Empty old timetable → `DEFAULT_SEMESTERS['1-1']` is preserved
- Old timetable with real entries → migrated into 1-1 as before
- 2-1 through 4-2 → unaffected

